From 1e788a3aa6b72a2f4a939a8d04b31496abe3bf77 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Dmitry Minkovsky <dminkovsky@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 16 Nov 2026 15:16:27 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 2/3] Read a work's children in one query

Android Auto built a work's children by joining its parts and its releases
in Kotlin, counted them, and paged the joined list it held. One SQL
statement now reads a page of a work's children, its parts and then the
releases that perform it, at the offset the car asks for, and a live count
of them in SQL tells the car when they change.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
